{
  "case_id": "2009-09-338",
  "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "JOEL D. McGORMLEY",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because this is a habeas case arising from a murder conviction obtained in the Michigan courts, the threshold question under AEDPA is whether there is any clearly established Supreme Court precedent that the Michigan Supreme Court objectively, unreasonably applied in rejecting Mr. Lett's claims that the trial court had abused its discretion in -- in discharging the jury due to deadlock."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Excuse me. The content of the first note was a query of the court. And that query was: \"What happens if we can't reach a verdict?\" Isn't that substantially different? Doesn't that suggest that the jury is trying to figure out what are the consequences of its actions and whether reaching a consensus is possible?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could you tell me what facts found by the lower courts or the trial courts show that the Court acted, quote, and this is from our earlier Perez case, the very first in this area, \"deliberately, responsibly, and not precipitously\" in declaring a mistrial. What in the facts you have recited -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: There was no -- there was no pause, you agree, between the foreperson's report and the court then said immediately afterward: The jury is dismissed. So there was no interval for an objection?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask you as a matter of Michigan practice, could the trial judge have interrogated the other jurors beyond the foreman and asked them what they thought about whether there was a deadlock?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "His conclusion that there was a deadlock was based on one question and one answer of one of the jurors, and that was the whole record supporting his decision; is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, what other circumstance is relevant? The fact that they raised their voices during deliberation, certainly that -- that doesn't cut any ice either way, does it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "McGormley",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well -- oh, I believe it does, because this Court has indicated in Arizona that -- that acrimony is a concern."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What evidence was there to the effect that the jury was not deadlocked?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You can't say, can you, that every time the jury records that it can't reach a verdict or it hasn't reached a unanimous verdict, that that's a legal deadlock requiring a mistrial, can you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "McCowan",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Habeas relief was properly granted. I would like to first answer Justice Ginsburg's somewhat easy question for me."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "McCowan",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "evidences that the trial judge at least considered that there were -- that there competing interests and -- and debated whether to -- to dismiss the jury, which is an extraordinarily drastic remedy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0001-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, what clear and convincing evidence is there here that there was not a deadlocked jury?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0001-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there any decision in this Court that says that under -- that in a case in which those four factors are present, that the trial judge may not grant a mistrial?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "McCowan",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0001-0014",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I believe that the case ultimately comes down to whether the Michigan Supreme Court unreasonably applied this Court's precedent in finding that the trial judge exercised -- that there was manifest necessity in the absence of the trial judge exercising sound discretion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, why is that -- why is that so? If Mr. Gordon thought that this jury was 11-to-1 for acquittal, do you think he would have been reluctant to ask for a sidebar and object to the granting of a mistrial?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. McCowan",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the lack of objection really doesn't do anything to fortify the conclusion that there was manifest necessity in these facts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "we are bound to accept the factual determination of the State court, unless you can show by clear and convincing evidence that that's wrong."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you suggesting that you need a precedent overruling a lower court decision before we could declare that something was unreasonable -- that our precedent was unreasonably applied?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. McGORMLEY",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7dbf7ca081a1-0003-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "this -- this Court has never overruled a manifest necessity determination due to a deadlocked jury."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-09-338",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "7dbf7ca081a1bf66378bfb24c8cfe7922b840c1a5509fde59b222a84d0af3941",
